sentences.l:
and many also others
sons in the hall both were raised and were born,
legitimate, from a wife;

and I led home a wife of men rich-in-allotments
on account of my excellence, since not a worthless one was I
nor war-shunning;

but now already everything has left (me),
yet all the same the stubble, at least, you, I think, looking at it,
to know;

And on the seventh, having gone up from Crete, broad,
we were sailing with the North Wind, a fresh, fine wind,
easily, as if down a stream;

There truly I on my part ordered my trusty companions
right there by the ships to stay and the ships to guard,
and scouts to the lookouts I urged to go;

and in among them bolt-delighting Zeus
an evil panic into my companions cast, and not one brought himself
to stand opposed;

but to me Zeus himself in my mind thus a thought
made—would that I had died and my doom met
right there in Egypt;

for still me woe received—
at once from my head the helmet, well-made, I put off
and the shield from my shoulders, and the spear I threw out away from my hand;

But when indeed the eighth to me, coming round, year came,
then indeed a Phoenician came, a man deceits knowing,
a gnawer, who indeed many evils to men had done;

for his dear son, having come upon me,
by cold and by weariness overpowered, led me to the house,
having raised me by the hand, until he reached the halls of his father;
and about me both a cloak and a tunic, as clothing, he put on me.
